{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And with a male.</b> Since we find [in Scripture] 'Behold, I lay last night with my father,' behold, there is a prohibition against both the active and passive partner. And Rav Hananel said, of blessed memory, that there is one who produces on his body something like the form of female flesh, and this is impossible by nature. And some say: a hermaphrodite. And all this trouble is because משכבי אשה is plural language and singular form — two acts of lying. And the correct view in my eyes is that the commandment is according to its plain sense, and the men of insight also imposed the death penalty for it. And Scripture chose a respectful manner of expression, just as 'do not approach' [euphemistically denotes the act]. And since the male was created to act and the female to be acted upon, Scripture warned not to reverse the words of HaShem. And there is 'lying' to emit semen; therefore the word משכבי is plural language. And it is not fitting to elaborate:" "And it stated <b>it is an abomination.</b> For it is an abhorrent thing to a holy soul, even to him by nature."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "Resolved רב חננאל as 'Rav Hananel' based on the standard spelling of the name; some witnesses read רבי instead of רב."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:47.453738044Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}